{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The cup magnets felt like a natural next choice because they combine magnetic attachment with screw mounting, connecting my recent magnetic hooks and fastener purchases.",
    "The rolling base and screw hooks connect to my earlier interest in moving equipment and hanging things, although neither meets an immediate need."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The magnetic stirrer and drill cutters serve completely different tasks from magnetic hooks; sharing the word magnetic does not make them useful to me.",
    "The printer, extrusion rails, wiring supplies, and brewing tubing assume projects I have not shown a need for. Buying small hardware does not mean I want to start those projects."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My magnetic-hook purchases seem to have been treated as interest in anything involving magnets, rather than in practical attachment and hanging.",
    "My fastener purchases seem to have been stretched into a broad interest in specialized workshop equipment and project supplies."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases cluster around hooks, attachment hardware, and fastener assortments; that shared practical purpose matters more than a broad connection to tools.",
    "I rarely choose something without a clear current use. Even related hanging hardware or moving equipment can be unnecessary, especially when the connection comes from an older purchase."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in practical attachments but extended it too far into unrelated equipment and projects."
}"}
